=====================================
FOLDER: TS_OPES
SYSTEM: MareNostrum 5 — glogin2
CREATED: 06/07/2026
UPDATED: 07/10/2026
PURPOSE: OPES runs exploring the transition-state region of the ppimg2
         (2Mg(2+)[P2O7](4-)) system with the ArcaNN iteration-006 NNP committee.
=====================================

06/07/2026

o OPES metadynamics runs exploring the transition-state region of the ppimg2
  system, using the ArcaNN iteration-006 NNP committee
  ('graph_1/2/3_006_compressed.pb', copied into each replica folder alongside the
  shared top-level copy). Each replica runs LAMMPS+DeepMD+PLUMED from
  'ppimg2-TS.lmp' via 'job_lammps_submission.sh', biasing the reaction coordinate
  defined in 'plumed_ppimg2-TS.dat', and logs 'COLVAR' and 'Coord_Mg.info'
  (Mg-coordination monitoring) plus 'model_devi.out' for committee-deviation QC.

o The files at the top level, outside the 'repN/' subfolders, are an earlier
  reference run of the same setup, predating the replica split. 'KERNELS' and
  'opes_md.dat' belong to that run.

01/10/2026

o Corrected the replica description. The previous version of this file stated
  "five replicas, same protocol with different seeds", which is the intent but not
  what is on disk. Checked each one:

    rep1  complete, 10 files, same file set as the reference run.
    rep2  complete, 10 files, identical layout to rep1 apart from the SLURM job id
          in the log name.
    rep3  PARTIAL, 4 files only. Missing the three NNP graph files, the LAMMPS
          input 'ppimg2-TS.lmp' and the log 'ppimg2-TS.log'. It cannot be rerun or
          analysed as it stands.
    rep4  EMPTY.
    rep5  EMPTY.

o So the usable statistics here are two replicas, not five. rep3 was set up and
  abandoned, rep4 and rep5 were only ever created as directories. If an analysis
  script globs 'rep*' and averages, it will silently average over two.

o rep1 and rep2 are genuinely consistent with each other, so they are described
  once here rather than carrying one README each.

07/10/2026

o Decision on the incomplete replicas: leave them exactly as they are. rep3 stays
  partial, rep4 and rep5 stay empty. Elia will look at them. They are not abandoned
  clutter to be cleaned, so do not remove or regenerate them, and keep remembering
  that an analysis globbing 'rep*' here averages over two usable replicas only.
